// Source: Source: Der Kreis (1951), p.136, Froschkonzert, folk melody, one voice. https://bilingualinjapan.home.blog/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/ganze-sommernc3a4chte-lang-a306.pdf
// Expanded instrumental arrangement. The established melody keeps all pitches, onsets, written durations, rests, tempo and meter. Original plucked/keyboard accompaniment remains; independent low strings sustain its bass line and violin/viola voice its explicitly simultaneous harmonies. Common chord tones are tied, not reattacked. Characteristic woodblock percussion marks phrase/rhythmic structure. Clarinet answers the first four-quarter motif as a short round. No choir is used. Standard GM/CC7=100; lead and accompaniment velocities balanced for the larger ensemble.
// Musicbox title: Froschgesang
